/**
 * Matrix product of two matrices.
 * Computes x*y in the linear-algebra sense; the column count of ``x`` must
 * equal the row count of ``y``, otherwise an error is raised. When either
 * argument is a scalar the result is the elementwise product instead. The
 * sparsity pattern of the result is the structural product of the patterns
 * (entries that are structurally zero in every term stay structural zeros).
 * For Sparsity arguments only the pattern of the product is computed.
 * Optional ``blas`` selects the BLAS plugin used for dense numeric kernels.
 * The choice only takes effect on numeric DM / MX dense * dense; symbolic
 * types (Sparsity, SX) and the sparse fallback path ignore it.
 * Values of ``blas:``
 * - ``reference`` (default): built-in reference kernel (triple loop)
 * - ``classic``: whatever BLAS was built into casadi via WITH_LAPACK (typically OpenBLAS)
 * - ``blasfeo``: BLASFEO
 * Plugins (``classic``, ``blasfeo``) are loaded lazily on first use; if the
 * corresponding plugin DLL isn't present in the build, calling them raises an
 * error.
 * Parameters:
 * x: Left factor
 * y: Right factor
 * blas: Name of the BLAS plugin for dense numeric products
 * Returns:
 * Matrix of size x.size1() by y.size2()
 * See also: mac, times, norm_0_mul
 * Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3v
 * Doc source:
 * https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1381
 * Implementation:
 * https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1381-L1384
 * 
 */
export function mtimes(x: Sparsity, y: Sparsity, blas?: string): Sparsity;
