/**
 * Remainder after division: (x,y) -> remainder(x,y)
 * This Function follows the convention of
 * https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/remainder:  x - n*y with n the
 * integer nearest to x/y (ties to even), so the result lies in [-|y|/2,
 * |y|/2].
 * Notably:
 * - remainder(5,3) -> -1
 * - remainder(5,-3) -> -1
 * - remainder(-5,3) -> 1
 * - remainder(-5,-3) -> 1
 * This is equivalent to Python's math.remainder. There is no equivalence in
 * Matlab. Elementwise, shape rules as for plus; structural zeros of ``x`` stay
 * zero.
 * See also: fmod  Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_24x
 * Doc source:
 * https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L2099
 * Implementation:
 * https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L2099-L2101
 * 
 */
